Gunship development build

Enhanced framerate (CUSTOM1) is off by default and requires a 68020 or
later. On a 68000 the option is ignored and native timing is retained.
All framerate enhancements use this master option.

The experimental TIMING_RUNTIME build adds a 3 Hz world clock, responsive
player motion and renderer-only object prediction. It remains in development;
ordinary builds retain native timing.

FS-UAE 68040 play setup

Use the cycle-exact 68040 core without MMU emulation for this development
build. The shared full-MMU a1200-040 preset corrupts the intro, menus and
cockpit with either CACHE or NOCACHE. The working configuration retains
asynchronous blits and enables the CPU data cache; immediate blits are not
required. This is an emulator configuration workaround, not a hardware fix.
With the shared a1200-040 preset (25 MHz, 2 MB chip, 8 MB fast), override:

  --cpu=68040-NOMMU --uae_cpu_cycle_exact=true
  --uae_cpu_memory_cycle_exact=true --uae_blitter_cycle_exact=true
  --uae_uaeboard=full

Use CUSTOM1=1 for Enhanced framerate. CACHE may remain enabled.
